  {"comment": "Page 6 of the painter's manual, selections and the transform tool. At 1280 by 1024 and an interface scale of 1, the size page 1 is shot at. The dockers are parked and three are placed, so every drag lands on the canvas. A small picture is painted with the brush, the toolbox's selection button is opened with a right press, an ellipse is drawn with Ellipse Select by a real drag, the Select menu's windows are opened by their rows, and the Transform tool turns what the ellipse holds. The shots are the pictures on manual/06-selections-and-the-transform-tool.md, and the dumps are where the page read every name it gives."},
